_platon_squeeze_details
;
 There is a single void in the lattice centered at an inversion center.
 The residual electron density on difference maps is quite low with maxima
 about 0.4 e-.  The void is sufficiently large to accomodate an additional 
 FAF molecule which would be required to be disordered about the inversion 
 center.  The calculated contribution of 126 electrons due to diffuse
 scattering is in good agreement with 136 electrons expected for the missing 
 molecule.
;
